# ==============================================================================
# Planora AI - Google OAuth 2.0 & Google Calendar Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================
#
# Follow these steps to obtain credentials from Google Cloud Console:
# 1. Visit: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create or select your Google Cloud project (e.g., "Planora AI").
# 3. Enable the "Google Calendar API":
#    APIs & Services -> Library -> Search "Google Calendar API" -> Click Enable.
# 4. Configure the OAuth Consent Screen:
#    APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen -> External -> Fill App Name & User Support Email.
#    Add Scopes:
#      - .../auth/userinfo.email
#      - .../auth/userinfo.profile
#      - openid
#      - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events
#      - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
#    Add Test Users (if app status is Testing): Add your Gmail (e.g. your_email@gmail.com).
# 5. Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID:
#    APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID
#    Application type: Web application
#    Name: Planora AI Web Client
#    Authorized JavaScript origins:
#      http://localhost:5500
#      http://127.0.0.1:5500
#    Authorized redirect URIs:
#      http://localhost:5500/auth/google/callback
#      http://127.0.0.1:5500/auth/google/callback
# 6. Copy the generated Client ID and Client Secret below:
# ==============================================================================

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id_here.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret_here
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5500/auth/google/callback

# Planora AI Server Port & Secret
PORT=5500
SESSION_SECRET=your_random_session_secret_here

# Optional: Universal AI Co-Pilot API Key (OpenAI, Google Gemini, Groq, Anthropic, etc.)
PLANORA_AI_KEY=

